Post a Claude Code session's first message while its sandbox starts.

Since upstream #8039, the first message of a Claude Code session stays in
the browser (initialDraft) until Claude Code reports its model, so Stop can
put it back in the composer before it reaches the agent. For a sandbox
session that's the whole start, a minute or more. On a phone, closing the
app in that time lost the message: it was never sent. Codex sessions never
waited.

modelSelectionPending no longer waits for Claude's model while the session's
sandbox is starting (sandboxStatus is set and not ready or failed). The
message is posted straight away and waits on the server, which delivers it
once the sandbox is up and, with
images/server/patches/0020-stop-message-waiting-for-sandbox.patch, lets Stop
take it back: the POST answers 409, so send() puts the draft back in the
composer. A pending model switch, and a session on your own machine, keep
the draft local as before.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d).
